{% extends "base.jinja2" %}

{% block content %}
## TASK
{% block category_task %}
{# Overridden by child templates (e.g., biographical vs toponymic) #}
{% endblock %}

## NARRATIVE ARCHITECTURE & STRUCTURE
{% block category_architecture %}
{# Overridden by child templates (e.g., chronological body vs geographic features) #}
{% endblock %}

## FORMATTING & HEADING RULES
- NEVER use '# ' (H1) or emit '## References' or '## MBRAS Sources'.
- Use '{{ body_heading_prefix }} ' for all thematic body subheadings.
- Conclude with '{{ body_heading_prefix }} Research and Documentation'.
- Ground all assertions using numeric citations [N] or [N, pp. X–Y] immediately following the factual claim.
- Attribute findings clearly to the respective scholars and observers.

## ARTICLE SCALE & PROPORTIONALITY CONTRACT
- TARGET LENGTH: Approximately {{ target_words }} words (adhere strictly to this scope).
- PROPORTIONALITY RULE: 
  {% if target_words < 600 %}
  This is a focused, limited archival record. Deliver a tight, high-density synthesis in 2–3 paragraphs under 1–2 subheadings. Do NOT artificially pad with background narrative or speculative filler.
  {% elif target_words > 1400 %}
  This is a major hub or regional cluster. Provide a thorough, multi-section survey covering all key facets and subtopics documented in the records.
  {% else %}
  This is a standard encyclopedic subject. Deliver a balanced, rigorous synthesis across 2–3 substantive thematic sections.
  {% endif %}

## STRICT SCOPE RESTRICTION:
- Never extrapolate broad regional, cultural, or biological generalisations that are not explicitly stated in the sources.
- If the records discuss only a single specimen, finding, or short notice, state the limits of the record immediately in Sentence 1.
- DO NOT invent statements about the subject's overall status, largest size, ecological role, or economic significance unless directly quoted or cited from the records.

## ARCHIVAL EVIDENCE RECORDS
{% for src in sources %}
[{{ loop.index }}] {{ src.author_display }} ({{ src.year }}). "{{ src.title }}". {{ src.journal_citation }}
{% if src.pages %}Pages: {{ src.pages }}{% endif %}
{% if src.lede %}
Context & Overview:
{{ src.lede }}
{% endif %}
{% if src.summary %}
Source Evidence:
{{ src.summary }}
{% endif %}
{% if src.key_findings %}
Key Findings:
{% for kf in src.key_findings %}
- {{ kf }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if src.context_notes %}
Archival Notes: {{ src.context_notes | join("; ") }}
{% endif %}

{% endfor %}

Write the encyclopedia article now:
{% endblock %}